    {
      "card_ids": ["C07"],
      "claim": "The hexafluoroisopropyl carbamate warhead in JW642 (M2) showed moderate BBB penetration in mice (SUV 0.2–0.8), providing some evidence that this carbamate motif can cross the BBB.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C09"],
      "claim": "A carbamate-containing analogue (M4) achieved a brain-to-plasma ratio of approximately 1 in rats, supporting some CNS access.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "moderate",
  "decision_summary": "The closest structural analogue (M1, similarity 0.5312) is experimentally impermeable/low brain-accumulating and shares the key azetidine-piperazine-thiazole scaffold, strongly supporting a fail prediction. The hexafluoroisopropyl carbamate warhead has moderate penetration evidence in less similar scaffolds, but the high-transfer direct evidence from M1 outweighs it.",
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct brain/plasma, CSF, or uptake measurement exists for the exact query molecule.",
    "The hexafluoroisopropyl carbamate warhead may alter transporter recognition or passive permeability relative to the closest amide analogue.",
